{
 "about": "The editor's Filters and Effects (docs/editor-plan.md section 5). Read by the editor (preview, WebGL) and by the render (hub/ingest/grade.py, ffmpeg), so the preview matches the finished video. A filter is a set of grade settings (see grade.js / grade.py); its strength blends between the original colour (0) and the full filter (1). Effects have a default strength. Adjustments are the primary correction applied before the filter: each slider value v (-1..1, 0 = off) becomes grade setting = base + v * scale (fade only uses v > 0). Filters marked \"instagram\" follow CSSgram's recreations of Instagram's filters (MIT, Una Kravets): CSS filter functions (\"css\") and colour layers blended on top (\"layers\": colour 0..1, blend mode, alpha, opacity), computed with the W3C formulas; radial/linear gradients in those recipes are reduced to their main colour (use Vignette for the edges). Approximations, not Instagram's own filters. Effects marked render_only are applied in the finished video only (the preview can't do them, e.g. Denoise is temporal).",
